From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: AVI InfoFrame says No Data (ITC=0) for
 content type No Data

big-fella: amdgpu's AVI InfoFrame says No Data (ITC=0) for content type No Data.

DC's set_avi_info_frame() sets ITC=1 for every content type, so the
connector's "content type" No Data (KWin's default in kwin-big-fella) goes out
as ITC=1, CN=0: Graphics. LG webOS then classifies the input as a PC
(aviContentType GRAPHICS, seen on the B4 with ryzen-fella). CTA-861: ITC=0
means no content type data; i915 sends that. Only the No Data case changes;
Graphics, Photo, Cinema and Game keep ITC=1 with their CN. See big-fella's
docs/dv-amd.md and docs/tv-pc-mode.md.

Regrouped from linux-9922-big-fella-amdgpu-avi-no-data (YBLOD 0.3.0 to
0.4.1); no code change.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
index a0fe0bde27c0..d878012231ca 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/core/dc_resource.c
@@ -5002,8 +5002,11 @@ static void set_avi_info_frame(
 
 	switch (stream->content_type) {
 	case DISPLAY_CONTENT_TYPE_NO_DATA:
+		/* big-fella: No Data is ITC=0, as CTA-861 and i915 have it;
+		 * ITC=1 with CN=0 says Graphics (LG TVs take the input for a PC).
+		 */
 		hdmi_info.bits.CN0_CN1 = 0;
-		hdmi_info.bits.ITC = 1;
+		hdmi_info.bits.ITC = 0;
 		break;
 	case DISPLAY_CONTENT_TYPE_GRAPHICS:
 		hdmi_info.bits.CN0_CN1 = 0;
